Condition : 5 - Prior to the commencement of development, a construction Environmental Management Plan (EMP) shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.

The EMP shall include details of the following during development:

"	Details of demolition/land raising/construction hours;
"	Dust suppression and monitoring measures, having regard to BRE guide 'Control of Dust from Construction and Demolition Activities';
"	Wheelwash measures;
"	Noise mitigation and monitoring measures;
"	Details of temporary lighting;
"	Details of enclosure of working areas;
"	A drainage strategy to operate setting out controls of contamination, including
controls to surface water run-off, water pumping, storage of fuels and hazardous materials, spill response plans and pollution control measures;
"	Pollution prevention and contingency measures;
"	Construction traffic management proposals including details of delivery routes and HGV movements and details of any temporary site access/parking;
"	Details of the location of compounds for the storage of plant and materials.

Development works shall be implemented in accordance with the approved EMP unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.
